#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/cli/getting_started.rst:3
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr "Getting started"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/cli/getting_started.rst:5
msgid ""
"The command line interface (CLI) is a useful utility for phpBB "
"administrators who have access to a shell (or SSH) on the server they run "
"phpBB on, as well as for extension developers. It provides CLI commands for "
"managing config values, extensions, running database migration, purging the "
"cache, and more."
msgstr ""
"The command line interface (CLI) is a useful utility for phpBB "
"administrators who have access to a shell (or SSH) on the server they run "
"phpBB on, as well as for extension developers. It provides CLI commands for "
"managing config values, extensions, running database migration, purging the "
"cache, and more."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/cli/getting_started.rst:7
msgid ""
"Most operating systems ship with a built in command line application. For "
"Mac OS and Ubuntu it is called \"Terminal\" and for Windows it is called "
"\"Command Prompt\". Third party software such as `PuTTY <http://www.putty."
"org>`_ and `iTerm <https://www.iterm2.com>`_ can also be used."
msgstr ""
"Most operating systems ship with a built in command line application. For "
"Mac OS and Ubuntu it is called \"Terminal\" and for Windows it is called "
"\"Command Prompt\". Third party software such as `PuTTY <http://www.putty."
"org>`_ and `iTerm <https://www.iterm2.com>`_ can also be used."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/cli/getting_started.rst:9
msgid ""
"To use phpBB's CLI on a web server, you will need SSH access to your web "
"server. You can find out from your web hosting company if they offer SSH "
"access and how to log into your web server from the CLI."
msgstr ""
"To use phpBB's CLI on a web server, you will need SSH access to your web "
"server. You can find out from your web hosting company if they offer SSH "
"access and how to log into your web server from the CLI."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/cli/getting_started.rst:11
msgid ""
"Once you have accessed your web server via SSH, or if you are in a localhost "
"development environment, you simply need to navigate to your phpBB forum "
"directory via the ``cd`` command:"
msgstr ""
"Once you have accessed your web server via SSH, or if you are in a localhost "
"development environment, you simply need to navigate to your phpBB forum "
"directory via the ``cd`` command:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/cli/getting_started.rst:17
msgid ""
"From there, issuing commands is simply a matter of calling phpBB's CLI "
"application."
msgstr ""
"From there, issuing commands is simply a matter of calling phpBB's CLI "
"application."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/cli/getting_started.rst:23
msgid ""
"*If everything is working correctly, the above command should output "
"information about the currently installed phpBB CLI console. If you receive "
"an error message, make sure you have navigated into the root directory of "
"your forum.*"
msgstr ""
"*If everything is working correctly, the above command should output "
"information about the currently installed phpBB CLI console. If you receive "
"an error message, make sure you have navigated into the root directory of "
"your forum.*"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/cli/getting_started.rst:26
msgid "General commands"
msgstr "General commands"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/cli/getting_started.rst:28
msgid ""
"The ``list`` command will show a list of all available commands available "
"for phpBB's CLI."
msgstr ""
"The ``list`` command will show a list of all available commands available "
"for phpBB's CLI."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/cli/getting_started.rst:34
msgid "The ``help`` command will display general help for using phpBB's CLI."
msgstr "The ``help`` command will display general help for using phpBB's CLI."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/cli/getting_started.rst:41
msgid "Using commands"
msgstr "Using commands"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/cli/getting_started.rst:43
msgid ""
"All phpBB commands (as described when running the ``list`` command) have "
"integrated help documentation available within the CLI. Use the ``--help`` "
"or ``-h`` option with any of phpBB's CLI commands to view detailed help for "
"that command."
msgstr ""
"All phpBB commands (as described when running the ``list`` command) have "
"integrated help documentation available within the CLI. Use the ``--help`` "
"or ``-h`` option with any of phpBB's CLI commands to view detailed help for "
"that command."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/cli/getting_started.rst:49
msgid ""
"The above command will display information about the arguments and options "
"that can be used with the specified command, in this example ``config:set``. "
"For example, the above command will output:"
msgstr ""
"The above command will display information about the arguments and options "
"that can be used with the specified command, in this example ``config:set``. "
"For example, the above command will output:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/cli/getting_started.rst:56
msgid ""
"Arguments or options shown inside of brackets indicates that they are "
"optional to use. This shows us that the ``key`` and ``value`` arguments are "
"required. However, the ``-d`` or ``--dynamic`` options available for this "
"command are optional. Also note that ``-d`` is shorthand for ``--dynamic``. "
"Most options have a shorthand equivalent."
msgstr ""
"Arguments or options shown inside of brackets indicates that they are "
"optional to use. This shows us that the ``key`` and ``value`` arguments are "
"required. However, the ``-d`` or ``--dynamic`` options available for this "
"command are optional. Also note that ``-d`` is shorthand for ``--dynamic``. "
"Most options have a shorthand equivalent."

